+++ b/docs/resonance-host-events.md
@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+# M495 PIS host events
+
+Enable RESONANCE_TEST, EMERGENCY_PARSER and PINPUT_RESONANCE_EVENTS in your
+own board configuration. PINPUT_RESONANCE_PROGRESS is optional. No option
+is enabled by applying this patch. RESONANCE_TEST requires a 32-bit CPU and
+an input-shaping configuration already supported by your Marlin version.
+
+M495 Q replies echo:PIS:RT:READY:1 without motion. M495 Q2 replies
+echo:PIS:RT:READY:2 without motion. Q1 is not an accepted command token.
+Both queries reject additional parameters. Existing uninstrumented M495
+and instrumented v1 sessions without W retain their previous behavior.
+
+For a v2 session, send M495 X F20 T60 O20 A40 I12345678 S W. The ID must be
+a canonical nonzero uint32. Marlin homes and positions without activating
+the generator, emits HOMED:<id>:<millis>, then ARMED_WAIT:<id>. The host
+starts its sensor and verifies fresh samples before sending M495 I12345678 R.
+ARM_ACK means the matching request was accepted; START precedes activation.
+All event lines have the echo:PIS:RT: prefix. COMPLETE is emitted only after
+the native motion buffers and pending FT step bits have drained.
+
+The 30-second ARM timeout starts on entry to WaitingArm. Missing or late ARM
+cannot start excitation. The dispatcher blocks conflicting commands while
+waiting. ID, port, timeout, cancellation, running/trusted-axis state and the
+prepared position/buffers are checked before authorization. M496 cancels
+preparation, waiting or excitation. Terminal responses are COMPLETE:<id>,
+ABORTED:<id> or ERROR:<id>:<reason>. A rejected ARM uses
+ARM_REJECTED:<id>:<reason>; it never starts a new sweep.
+
+Sensor failure after ARM requires M496 and a matching terminal response even
+if the host has not received START. UART cannot detect an instantaneous host
+disconnect after accepted ARM. No automatic restart is provided. Keep direct
+LCD/other-host actions from changing the machine during a measurement.
+
+No serial output or blocking host wait is added to the ISR. Native resonance
+equations and FT Motion internals are unchanged. Run the actual-source host
+harness with:
+
+```bash
+python3 buildroot/tests/resonance_host_events/test_protocol.py
+```
+
+Also compile and validate your board configuration before physical use.
